 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Fighting passage: anchored in its history (the Tabuk expedition, 9 AH); the command itself is not glossed; no battle, weapon, march or army drawn; no present-day reading and no people targeted. No motif on the Prophet ﷺ. 38:1-3 dates the passage (As-Sa'di: revealed about Tabuk) and 38:6-12 gives its hardship; 39:1-5 keeps As-Sa'di's restriction «في حال الاستنفار» (when the call to march is made). As-Sa'di's «ثم لا يكونوا أمثالكم» (47:38 word for word) is not used. A moon for the months, night and day for «يحلونه عاما ويحرمونه عاما», a house for «اثاقلتم إلى الأرض», wind for the fleeting enjoyment. STAGING v4: c1 (37, the postponed months) stays ambient: the tafsirs give the practice and its aim (fighting in the sacred months), not how or where it was done, so nothing is drawn. The old chapter 38-39 is split: c2 (38) is staged in a town by day: one group of three believers at the centre (the reproached; As-Sa'di: some of the Muslims were heavy; a single small group, so it does not stand for all the believers, and no two groups face each other like two armies); nobody calls them (the call came from the Prophet: camera only on 38:6-12) and nobody marches or carries anything: no call to fight is pictured; on 38:13 the group sits down (Al-Muyassar: you were heavy and kept to your homes) under a house plate, the camera tilts to the ground on 38:15, and a falling-leaf plate for the little enjoyment of this world (38:22). c3 (39, new title) stays ambient: a conditional threat, the replacing with another people (not drawn) and Allah's power; geometric mood (His acts) and a geometric plate on the Name (39:12). The background of c3 stays quiet on 39:3-8."
 },
